KG42.register("clusters-0aab3787674f3fad4ce77202",{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v142-d-CL002","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","label":"CDA matching, execution pricing, and order maintenance for time-of-use electrical energy orders","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"CDA matching, execution pricing, and order maintenance for time-of-use electrical energy orders","market_meaning":"Within the CDA protocol period of the corresponding time slot, the trading platform receives asynchronous orders, sorts them by price and arrival time, matches buyers and sellers with compatible prices, determines the executed quantity and execution price, and maintains incomplete orders; net load also provides a quantity input for demand orders.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01-p2p-cda"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination","matching","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"All chains belong to the same community CDA, but the quantity and price interfaces must correspond to the same time slot, the same order, and the same matching state. The execution price is interpreted according to the specific match, and the time-slot notation cannot be used to infer uniform pricing for all executions. The order quantity unit and the treatment of sell orders after an equal-quantity execution remain unresolved.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is from order entry into the trading platform to the formation of a trade with explicit quantity and price and the maintenance of the order book, jointly presenting submission, coordination, matching, clearing, and pricing functions. R003 is retained as the clearing perspective on matched quantity and is not counted as an additional independent execution rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the demand quantity input, as well as the post-execution buy-order update and removal branches."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the post-execution sell-order update and removal branches; the missing rule for initial sell-order quantity is disclosed separately."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Retain the executed-quantity expression under the demand-side and supply-side clearing perspectives, and display it in association with the same matched-quantity relationship in R006."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Clarify the input process by which buy and sell orders asynchronously arrive at the trading platform."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carry the trading platform's responsibility, alternate arrival triggers, sorting, compatibility checks, and trade formation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Determine the trade price for successful matches, completing the price outcome of the trade."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Define the community time-of-use electrical energy product to which the orders and trades correspond."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06"],"rationale":"The time-of-use electrical energy product defines the trading object of arriving orders; the source further states that each target time slot has a corresponding order book."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E10"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that after orders arrive and are entered into the book, the trading platform attempts matching; buy-order arrival and sell-order arrival are respectively substitutable triggers."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_b_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"rationale":"The current requested quantity of the same buy order enters the calculation of the executed quantity for that local match; this interface does not resolve the unit issue from net load to electrical energy quantity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_s_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"The current supplied quantity of the same sell order enters the calculation of the executed quantity for that local match, and the subsequently updated quantity still needs to retain its state time point."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E11"],"rationale":"The three constraints contain the same price-compatibility condition and executed-quantity relationship; R006 additionally carries the trade-formation semantics, and the attribution of each original function is retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_matched_t"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"rationale":"After a successful execution, the buy order enters the remaining-quantity update or completed-removal branch according to the quantity relationship between the two executed parties; when matching is unsuccessful, these branches cannot be executed based on quantity comparison alone."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_matched_t"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"rationale":"Sell-order update and removal share successful matching as a common condition; the existing R002 covers only the two branches of strict inequality, and the equal-quantity case is retained as a gap."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CON08","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E11"],"rationale":"The source writes the matched quantity and the corresponding execution price together into the transaction agreement of the buyer and seller, so matching and pricing jointly express the formation of one trade."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"Both refer to the same CDA demand-order function; only a display representative is selected, and the constraints and edges in the original chains continue to be retained independently."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R009::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"Both are references to the same CDA supply-order function and do not change the arrival, matching, pricing, and maintenance responsibilities borne by each chain."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R002::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"All three places involve the same CDA execution allocation and its order-maintenance results; they are not merged with the node of the same name in ancillary service procurement."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"rationale":"In the source, the responsible entity for receiving orders and attempting matching is the community exchange in both cases, and the scope of application is the same."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x001","v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_b_t","v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-sigma-b"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"Under the same buy order and the same pre-matching state, both refer to the requested electrical energy quantity; their local roles as submitted quantity, sell-order update input, and matching input are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T001","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x002","v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_s_t","v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-sigma-s"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E09"],"rationale":"The supplied electrical energy quantity of the same sell order before the same match serves as a parameter or an operating variable in different chains; only a quantity correspondence is established, without rewriting its local type or role."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_sigma_matched_t","v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-sigma-matched"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07"],"rationale":"The two represent the executed electrical energy quantity of one execution for the same compatible buyer-seller pair and are not interpreted as the cumulative executed volume for the entire time slot."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_pi_b_t","v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-pi-b","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-pi-b-t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E08"],"rationale":"In the same execution event, the buy-order price is used both for the compatibility check and for execution pricing; different buy orders or quote-revision time points are not treated as equal on this basis."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::x_pi_s_t","v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-pi-s","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-pi-s-t"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E08"],"rationale":"In the same execution event, the sell-order price is used both for the compatibility check and for execution pricing; the different local input roles are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM10","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E11"],"rationale":"The price-compatibility condition and the executed-quantity expression are the same; the membership attributions of the demand side, supply side, and trade formation differ, so only the mathematical overlap is associated, and the entire constraint semantics is not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM11","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C002"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E08"],"rationale":"The two items give the same pricing expression and applicable conditions for the same executed buyer-seller pair; only one formula is selected as the display representative, and both parties' input edges and the original constraints are retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R001 directly uses the optimized net load described in kW as the buy-order electrical energy quantity described in kWh, and the time conversion is not explained; a symbolic correspondence must not be regarded as dimensional closure.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T002","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the power, electrical energy, and time-step conventions in the source text, and have upstream explicitly revise them if necessary; D does not add multiplication by duration or change units."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R002 does not include the condition for the initial sell-order quantity corresponding to negative net load, and the existing content only maintains sell orders after execution. Optimized dispatch in this cluster is also only an external input to R001, and it cannot be claimed on this basis to cover complete customer bid generation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T002","v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement the verified initial supply submission rule and clarify the boundary of the dispatch model as an external input; keep the existing chains unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"For an equal-quantity execution, there is a discrepancy between the main text's statement that fully matched orders are removed and the appendix transcription in which the else branch retains a zero-quantity sell order. R001 covers buy-order removal, and the strict-inequality branch of R002 does not resolve the state of that sell order; the sell-order construction in the appendix also contains a buyer identifier, which cannot be automatically normalized.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g04-E03"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the equal-quantity branch, zero-quantity order handling, and order identity in the main text and appendix, and then handle the discrepancy through an explicit upstream revision."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"All evidence in this cluster remains independently unverified; the cited main text and appendix can support only provisional assembly and cannot prove that the transcription or algorithm has passed scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g04-E03"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Follow-up manual verification should check the cited sources, conditions, and object correspondences, especially the consistency between the main text and the appendix."}]},"rule_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R003","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R004","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R009","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R010"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-230dbf46f02b4bfe","COMP-c98744ae891e04fd","COMP-ffbf050cce03a2e6","KG31-69ba805a251afd65","KG40-12aedc3eec573697","KG40-20f45ec4bdcbac06","KG40-404d7eddbf0fc37c"]});
